=== GIL Demonstration ===
This demonstrates how GIL affects CPU-bound vs IO-bound tasks

=== Single Thread Execution ===
Single-Thread starting CPU-bound task...
Single-Thread completed in 0.60 seconds. Result: 333333283333335000000
Single-Thread starting CPU-bound task...
Single-Thread completed in 0.57 seconds. Result: 333333283333335000000
Total single-thread time: 1.17 seconds

=== Multiple Threads Execution ===
Thread-1 starting CPU-bound task...
Thread-2 starting CPU-bound task...
Thread-2 completed in 1.10 seconds. Result: 333333283333335000000
Thread-1 completed in 1.15 seconds. Result: 333333283333335000000
Total multi-thread time: 1.15 seconds

=== IO-bound Tasks with Threading ===
IO-Thread-1 starting IO-bound task...
IO-Thread-2 starting IO-bound task...
IO-Thread-3 starting IO-bound task...
IO-Thread-1 completed IO-bound task
IO-Thread-2 completed IO-bound task
IO-Thread-3 completed IO-bound task
IO-bound threading time: 2.00 seconds

Key Observations:
1. CPU-bound tasks don't benefit much from threading due to GIL
2. IO-bound tasks benefit significantly from threading
3. For CPU-bound tasks, consider multiprocessing instead

